! Gift-Bearer: Lares (Tasked Spirit) — the offering door, hand-back

Branch `feature/green-jello-dinosaur-5--offering` (cut at c0e0622a2), pushed. Commits: `8a87ed2fe` (the offering door), `723a0e1f6` (charter-seat retire + floor-cut test, after the controller re-ruled fork 4), `b8d128f4b` (merge of the span head 3156b4e94, clean), and a final narration cure.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-loop-as-built`>>

!! The loop, as built

OFFER → PROMOTE → RELEASE → ACCEPT → READ.

* ''Offer.'' `offerCanonRecords` (mesh). The lit face reads each named title off its own working layer (`wikis/<slug>/working`, its realm workbench) and opens a body `{kind, nexus, bag, face, offerer, records}`. Each record carries its fields, its digest (`carrierHashOf`) and a fork base (`overrideBase` of the working copy, or null). The face atom signs the body; the CID is sha-256 of the canonical body bytes. The offer lands as `$:/lar/canon-offer/<cid>` on the Nexus's offer table (`canonOfferDocUrl(nexus)`). Canon never moves. Replaying the same offer gives the same CID and `landed: false`.
* ''Review.'' `readCanonOffers` and `showCanonOffer` give each record's freshness: `new` · `base-holds` · `landed` · `canon-is-fresher`, plus field diffs. "canon is fresher" is a warning only.
* ''Promote.'' `promoteCanonOffer` calls `requireKahuReach(bag)` ''first'', so a non-steward gets `kahu-reach` and nothing is read or written. If the base moved and the steward passed no `overFresher`, it refuses `offer-base-moved`. Otherwise it writes the offered bytes into the canon CRDT and adds a steward-signed retire `$:/lar/canon-offer-retired/<offerCid>`. The offer row stays. Replaying a promotion hits the retire and lands nothing.
* ''Release.'' `cutReleaseFloor` (mesh) cuts the next floor from live canon. It re-cuts each slug the prior floor names, keeps the prior snapshot for any slug with no live doc here, and stages blobs before the manifest is written. On node this is the `floor-cut` store-door row, run by `lares nexus release <manifest-file> --cut`. After that the existing `nexus promote open|sign` and `nexus release --approval` run unchanged. If canon hasn't moved, the cut returns the prior manifest's own CID.
* ''Accept + read.'' These are Leap 1's `acceptFloorRelease` and `resolveFloor`/`floorReadFace`, unchanged. The composition test proves h1 reads the promoted record.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/shared-seam-and-adapters`>>

!! Shared seam and adapters

* ''Seam:'' `packages/lararium-mesh/src/canon-offer.ts` holds every decision and the port compositions. It adds `cutCanonFloor` in `floor-manifest.ts`, `canonOfferDocUrl` in `deterministic-doc.ts`, and the domains `canon-offer` and `canon-offer-retire` in `domains.ts`.
* ''Daemon skins (both hosts):'' `packages/lararium-tw5/src/canon-offer-verbs.ts` defines `offer-make` · `offer-list` · `offer-show` · `offer-promote`. `packages/lararium-keyhive/src/operator-daemon-behavior.ts` registers them; the node and browser daemon islands both run that file. The ports bind by capability:
** working and canon access through `makeBagAccess` (now exported from `action-handler.ts`);
** the canon write only after `requireKahuReach` over the vessel's Kahu source;
** the board through `materializeSharedLarDoc(canonOfferDocUrl)`;
** the face atom as signer.

The Nexus is the only binding that differs by host: node reads it off the shore's charter (`kahuCabal`); browser takes the call's own `nexus` arg (its island reads no charter). A named Nexus that differs from the charter's refuses `offer-foreign-nexus`.
* ''Node adapter:'' `packages/lararium-node/src/commands/floor-cut.ts` plus the `floor-cut` row in `store-door-verbs.ts`.
* ''CLI:'' `lares meme offer <uri…> --bag <slug>` · `offer list [--bag] [--all]` · `offer show <cid>` · `offer promote <cid> [--over-fresher]` in `commands/meme.ts`. `lares nexus release <file> --cut` is in `commands/nexus-release.ts`. Help, accepts rows and `BOOLEAN_FLAGS` (`over-fresher`) are updated. No new top-level verb.
* ''MCP:'' `meme_offer` · `meme_offer_list` · `meme_offer_show` in `lares_mcp.py`, all HOTL. Promote has no tool: it stays the steward's hand. Also updated: `OFFER_VERBS`, `gen_cli_verbs.mjs` CLI_FORMS, the regenerated `fixtures/cli-verbs.json`, and the tool-set union in `test_lares_mcp.py`.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/red-tests`>>

!! Red tests (each run alone, `--maxWorkers=2`)

* `packages/lararium-mesh/tests/canon-offer.test.ts` — 10 pass:
** an unadmitted face offers and canon stays unmoved;
** withheld/`cap/**` titles refuse, and a forged row carrying one is set aside;
** a replayed offer lands nothing;
** a non-steward promote refuses for 4 stranger kinds;
** the steward promotes and retires;
** a replayed promote lands nothing;
** a moved base warns, refuses, then lands on the explicit choice;
** the full loop: offer h1 → promote h0 → `cutReleaseFloor` → `assembleFloorRelease` → `acceptFloorRelease` → `floorReadFace` reads the record;
** node (Automerge board and canon doc) and browser (memory) reach the same decision;
** a digest guard.

These were red while the module was absent. I also checked by mutation: removing the reach call, the retire hold, the fresher refusal, the replay guard, or the cap-path law each turns its named test red.
* `packages/lararium-tw5/tests/canon-offer-verbs.test.ts` — 3 pass. Through the real reactors: offer → stranger promote refuses `kahu-reach` (also fail-closed with no source) → steward promotes → replay holds. A `cap/**` title refuses as data, and a faceless floor refuses `waking-floor`. Node (charter Nexus) and browser (call-named Nexus) reach the same decision through the same reactor; foreign and absent Nexus refuse.
* `packages/lares-cli/tests/meme-offer-plan.test.ts` — 2 pass (routing and usage refusals).
* I touched these, ran each alone, and they stay green: lares-cli `parse-args`, `laws/accepts-track-the-handlers`, `help-flags`, `laws/routing-follows-declaration`; node `floor-door`.
* Each test file typechecks under its package config (temporary tsconfig, removed afterwards).
* ''Not run green:'' `packages/lararium-sensorium/scripts/test_lares_mcp.py`. 4 tests fail on `ModuleNotFoundError: mcp.server.mcpserver` in this venv, which is an environment fault and not caused by the edit. I checked parity statically instead: `mirrored` equals the tool tuples and every tool has a seat.

