<<~ ahu slot=`#/forks-decided`>>

!! Forks decided (moʻolelo, each overrulable; full text in offering.mem #/the-canon-offer)

# ''Where an offer rests: an offer table beside the Kahu realm, one per Nexus.'' Gaia 2026: patches go to a subsystem list, versus PRs from scattered forks. Elyncia 5492: the votive table at the temple's door, versus a pilgrim walking into the sanctum. Fable's realm-drafts lean would either seat h1/h2 inside the Kahu realm (the ruling withholds that) or fork the ruling. An outbox leaves the steward no derivable place to look across vessels. This reopens if realm drafts gain an append-only, non-member write class.
# ''Fork base = the working copy's own `overrideBase`, never canon's current carrier at offer time.'' A copy that never forked from canon reads "canon is fresher" wherever canon holds the title.
# ''A stale promote refuses `offer-base-moved` until `--over-fresher`.'' The retire records the fresher canon digests it overrode. No auto-merge.
# ''A retire's authority is its signature plus the offer-CID key.'' A forged retire can only hide an offer from the open list (`--all` still shows it); it can never move canon, which only moves under the reach.
# ''The verb lives at `lares meme offer …`.'' `lares meme promote` already names the residency crossing.
# ''The browser names its Nexus per call.'' A browser promote fails closed because it holds no Kahu board.
# ''The floor cut is `nexus release --cut`.'' `cut` was already a boolean flag; the manifest path stays positional.

<<~/ahu>>

