<<~ ahu slot=`#/round-two-the-controller-s-three-asks`>>

!! Round two — the controller's three asks

# ''Fork 4 re-ruled: a forged retire hides nothing.''
#* A retire now carries the charter's epoch lineage, the way a floor release does.
#* Every reader (fold, list, show, the promote decision) honours a retire only where `rosterOfLineage(nexus, lineage, epoch)` proves the roster of its epoch and the signer holds a seat in that roster.
#* Any other retire reads `retire-unauthorised` and the offer stays open. `offer show` names the refused retire and its signer, and `offer list` notes it.
#* Rows are keyed `<offer cid>/<retire cid>`, so a forgery written first can't occupy the steward's key.
#* ''Why a charter seat stands for "the steward's hand":'' an atom key names no group a reader can verify without a persona KEL; a seat proves itself in the lineage.
#* ''Split this forced:'' the seat keys live in the vault beside the store door, not in the daemon island. So `offer-promote` (daemon verb, Kahu reach first) now only writes canon. The retire is the new store-door row `offer-retire` (`packages/lararium-node/src/commands/offer-retire.ts`), which calls `retireCanonOffer`. That function:
#** refuses `offer-not-landed` until canon carries every digest;
#** refuses `offer-retire-unseated` before signing with an unseated key.
#* `lares meme offer promote` runs both steps. If the retire can't land, it says so and exits non-zero (canon write stands, offer stays open).
#* ''Red test:'' "a stranger-signed retire leaves the offer open". It covers a stranger's key with the true lineage and a seat of a different charter. As a control, the real seat still retires afterwards. Proven by mutation: dropping the seat check turns it red.
#* ''Known edge, in canon:'' a retire names its own epoch, so a seat removed by a later roll could still retire under the epoch it held.
# ''Node unit test for the floor cut:'' `packages/lararium-node/tests/floor-cut.test.ts`, 4 passing. `runFloorCut` now binds through a testable `runFloorCutOver`. The test covers:
#* the promoted row riding the cut, a slug with no live doc keeping its snapshot, and the floor standing whole in the CAS with the file holding the exact manifest bytes;
#* an unmoved cut returning the prior CID;
#* an absent prior refusing `floor-cut-refused` with no file written;
#* a source check that `runFloorCut` goes through `runFloorCutOver`.
# ''Merge:'' origin/feature/green-jello-dinosaur-5 (3156b4e94) merged cleanly. Re-run alone afterwards:
#* mesh canon-offer: 11
#* tw5 canon-offer-verbs: 3
#* node floor-cut: 4, floor-door: 3
#* cli meme-offer-plan, accepts-track, parse-args, help-flags: green
#* bcc 807 ok; doctype ok; domain-registry ok; typecheck witness clean
#* Evergreen read narration 163/162 after the merge. I reworded one doc line in canon-offer.ts and it went back to 162/162.

